# The working tree is edited from Windows/OneDrive while the history was
# committed with mixed endings.  Normalising to LF in the repository keeps
# `git status` honest; checkouts are unaffected on Linux/macOS and Git
# converts on the fly for Windows checkouts if core.autocrlf=true.
#
# NOTE: this attribute alone does not rewrite what is already committed.
# To renormalise once (single, reviewable commit):
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "normalise line endings"
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz  binary
*.gif binary
